 pill showed \"Daily Amount exceeded / For tomorrow $1.6\". At 7:43 before saving (right after opening entry mode), the pill showed \"$1.9\" (only amount). Hmm, the first ever screenshot at launch showed \"Today | $1.9\". Hmm.\n\nWait, at 7:44 first entry screenshot (before typing) showed \"$1.9\" centered only, no \"Today\". Hmm, maybe because \"Today\" label is animated out when the expense entry is focused? Not sure.\n\nThis might be the pill bug: when opening the entry screen/keypad, the \"Today\" label disappears, showing only the amount. Is that expected? The changed item: \"Main screen budget pill: the remaining amount is now computed from the current budget period.\" So the amount is what matters; the label missing might be a separate cosmetic bug. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the current entry screen: elements [1] shows \"Daily Amount exceeded | For tomorrow $1.6\". At launch it was \"Today | $1.9\". So the pill content is contextual.\n\nLet me now check the pill by entering an amount smaller than the daily. Since today's spending already exceeds, the pill always shows exceeded. To test the pill properly, I'd need today's spending below the daily; but we already added $8 today, and the daily is $1.9. So the pill shows exceeded. That's consistent.\n\nHmm, but wait: the pill says \"Daily Amount exceeded\" the moment the app opens (before we entered anything)? At launch, the pill showed \"Today | $1.9\" — so today's spent was $0 and remaining $1.9. After we entered $8, \"Daily Amount exceeded\". Fine.\n\nWait, was today's $8 really saved? The list showed \"Today Food 07:44 AM $8\". Yes.\n\nNow let me test undo/reversal of an expense: can I delete/edit the saved $8 expense? Tap on the expense in the list to see options. This tests \"Reversal\". Let me collapse the keypad and tap the \"Food $8\" expense. Swipe down first."}
