he chips that appear *inside* the calculated amount card, like \"This week | Last week\"? Hmm.\n\n   Actually, maybe tapping the \"Calculated amount\" card opens the breakdown sheet; the change about chips might relate to the breakdown sheet's \"Daily/Weekly/Biweekly\" chips if they exist. But the breakdown dialog doesn't have chips.\n\n   Alternatively, the \"period breakdown chips\" might be in the Analytics screen's period selector (Days/Week/Biweek/Total) — those are chips for period breakdown! But the change says \"Budget sheet period breakdown chips\". Hmm, no.\n\n3. Split view selector active view stored in view-model memory — found not persisted (confirmed). Good.\n\n4. New keypad component — leading zero bug (dev couldn't repro). Maybe the actual seeded bug is elsewhere: e.g., key input lost/duplicated under rapid input, decimal handling, backspace not working, calculator result wrong, etc.\n\nLet me test the keypad more aggressively:\n- Rapid multi-digit entry (does every key register?)\n- Decimal handling (0.01, 1.005)\n- Operator chaining\n- Leading zeros (e.g., \"00\")\n- Pressing \"=\" with no operator\n- Pressing \".\" twice\n- Very long input\n- Input after saving (state reset)\n- Rotation (state loss?)\n- Device rotate during entry\n\nLet me investigate the keypad carefully. Start with a fresh entry screen. Currently the snackbar is present maybe. Let me observe."}
