early\"? No.\n\nOr maybe the \"budget sheet\" is the \"Calculated amount\" breakdown popup — it shows a \"period breakdown\" calculation. The \"chips\" could be the bottom keypad number keys? No.\n\nHmm. Let me search the UI for elements with multiple items in a row: Daily/Weekly/Biweekly (budget sheet), Ask me/Spread all/Day 1 lump (behavior), Days/Week/Biweek/Total (Analytics), Transport/Food/Category (entry), Forecast? These are all segmented chips.\n\nMaybe \"period breakdown chips\" = the Analytics screen's Days/Week/Biweek/Total chips (period breakdown of spending). The change item might have been written loosely (\"Budget sheet\" as in the budget-related sheet?). Hmm. The Analytics screen is out of the sweep area but is where period breakdown happens.\n\nGiven ambiguity, let me test the Analytics chips: tap each and see if the selected state and chart update. If a tap doesn't work, report.\n\nAlso, the Analytics screen has \"Categories\" toggle and \"Trend\". Hmm.\n\nLet me dismiss the breakdown dialog and go to Analytics. Actually, before that, note that the split view state resets to Daily when the sheet is reopened — reported. The dev confirmed. Good.\n\nI think the primary seeded bugs might be:\n1. Split view not persisted (confirmed).\n2. Maybe the budget sheet's calculated amount not updating when the amount changes? We saw the daily $1.9 stays while the breakdown shows today's vs tomorrow's. Hmm.\n3. Maybe the \"period breakdown chips\" tap issue is that tapping the chips *inside* the budget sheet's breakdown dialog... no chips.\n4. Keypad leading zero.\n\nHmm, let me approach differently: test the *privacy mode* interaction with the pill and keypad? No.\n\nLet me test the pill when the entry amount is entered: the pill shows \"$0.9\" etc. Is that computed from the current budget period? Yes. But what if the period's remaining budget is negative? Not testable.\n\nLet me test the budget pill *long-press* when the entry has an amount — the breakdown dial